   36 ## Confirmed goals versus proposed mechanisms
   37 
   38 Confirmed: evolve existing `swarm.config.json` to **`pipeline.config.json`**;
   39 `pipeline.json` and `--pipeline` remain project/workflow graph inputs. One
   40 editable author per setting/active owner/registration/instance/profile. No code,
   41 schema, ENV, CLI, Chart or entrypoint may supply missing migrated operator values.
   42 Migrate existing Swarm architecture rather than invent a second system index.
   43 No D18 worker refactor, paid Eval, host intervention or test reclassification.
   44 
   45 Proposed author root: repo `config/`, separated from Helm/Docker projections.
   46 This is justified only together with real packaging migration: Helm `.Files.Get`
   47 cannot read outside its packaged chart; `.dockerignore` and image change filters
   48 must include the selected immutable generation. Retaining current chart-root
   49 authors is technically possible, but obscures non-Chart component ownership and
   50 still requires profile materialization. The proposal chooses one root and one
   51 materializer, not two synchronized editable copies. Existing owner names remain
   52 unless a specific consumer contract requires a change.
   53 
   54 `config/pipeline.config.json` owns composition and selected profile references,
   55 not component setting values. Complete owner profiles live in service/engine/core
   56 files, plugin profiles by actual manifest identity and registration/instance.
   57 Agent profiles refer to supported provider/model/prompt resources. Shared
   58 endpoints/identity/storage grants belong to explicit deployment/runtime owners;
   59 consumer quotas and task parameters are not silently shared by matching names.
   60 Versions stay in the established version authority; external secret bytes are
   61 never included in inventory, explanation, snapshots or normal author files.
   62 
   63 ## Activation and instance contracts
   64 
   65 - **S, service/process**: ports, transport roots, trust, storage, concurrency
   66   pools and endpoints activate by validated startup/drain/restart. A running
   67   server is not changed by a stage profile refresh.
   68 - **R, run**: graph, module membership, grants, provider ABI, issuer, recovery
   69   foundations, total budget ceilings and mode are immutable for that run.
   70 - **M, module**: only eligible tuning/agent/model/prompt/quality profile fields
   71   select a new generation before the next unbound module, within R constraints.
   72   Implementation, repairs and all associated lint/review/test attempts share it.
   73 - **J, operation/plan**: standalone Prism order or Buster plan binds before
   74   admission/dispatch; children inherit it rather than independently reading Latest.
   75 - **V, nonsetting**: protocol/version/generated binding/task data retains its
   76   actual owner and reason. A literal is not exempt just because it is convenient.
   77 
   78 S/R/J/M is assigned per field after tracing its consumer. Fixed Eval selects one
   79 complete generation for all units; a scenario/dataset/scorer is task input, not
   80 permission to alter grants or reset budgets. No generic Evalrunner is claimed.
   81 Instance selection is by owner + registration + stable instance ID + explicit
   82 complete profile; existence of a profile does not activate a plugin or grant it
   83 capabilities. No implicit first profile, ENV override, missing-value coercion,
   84 fallback model or automatic old-filename lookup. An explicitly configured model
   85 fallback list is policy; actual selected model must be recorded and supported by
   86 the real adapter, not assumed from a profile label.
   87 
   88 ### Current dispatch codec versus target policy
   89 
   90 The current SDK `RuntimeDispatchProfile` is exactly
   91 `{schemaVersion: 'runtime-dispatch-profile.v1', encoding: 'json-utf16-v1'}`;
   92 `parseRuntimeDispatchProfile` compares canonical bytes. It is codec/control
   93 metadata, not an actual target/model/budget selector or a CONFIG-generation
   94 binding. At `openclaw-adapter.activate`, `targetsFrom(context.config)` captures
   95 the configured target map; `createDispatchAdapter.invoke` selects its actual
   96 target by `request.resource.canonicalId`, or rejects `RUNTIME_TARGET_DENIED`.
   97 Reviewer model/runtime/agent/thinking assertions and cache identity must not be
   98 described as dispatch selection merely because their names resemble settings.
   99 
  100 The proposed M binding must carry the actual complete supported target policy
  101 within unchanged R grants/canonical identity and persist it before dispatch.
  102 The existing two-field SDK codec cannot be repurposed as that closure or silently
  103 extended with model/generation fields. This corrects earlier working-evidence
  104 wording, which is retained separately as superseded history; no implementation
  105 or current durable M-selection mechanism is claimed.
