  107 ## Actual module and recovery source paths
  108 
  109 `skills/nova/project/compiler.ts::moduleStages` creates `implement-<module.id>`,
  110 `lint-<module.id>`, optional `review-<module.id>` and `test-<module.id>`;
  111 request-fix routes return to implementation. `source.ts`, `coverage.ts` and
  112 `demo.ts` generate source/architecture, cumulative integration and handoff stages.
  113 Current `module.id` is input identity, not a universal runtime config binding.
  114 Free graphs therefore need explicit versioned stage-membership metadata; do not
  115 guess modules from stage names or reload separately for each stage/HTTP request.
  116 
  117 `engine-run.ts::runNewPipeline` prepares runtime, enters `withRunMutationLock`,
  118 writes `run-snapshot.v4`, then calls `executePrepared`. `engine-snapshots.ts`
  119 publishes by exclusive temp write, file fsync, no-replace hardlink and directory
  120 fsync. `executePrepared` verifies graph and checks uncertain effects before
  121 starting adapters and runner. Recovery verifies the stored package set/digests
  122 and the captured registry configuration (not every PlatformConfig field), recovers lifecycle state and reconciles durable
  123 observability. These existing checks must not simply be removed for dynamic config.
  124 
  125 `stage-executor.ts` passes `definition.config`, creates a lease and appends
  126 `attempt.created` / `attempt.dispatched` before plugin invocation. Its current
  127 attempt record contains retry/remediation usage and lease identity but no
  128 separate module generation closure. `state/journal.ts::FileJournal` provides
  129 mutex-serialized, hash-chained fsync append/transact and rejects rewind/drift.
  130 This is synchronous exclusion, not multi-record rollback: a record appended
  131 before a callback throws remains committed. Fully validate before the one binding
  132 append; never await inside its callback. Seven
  133 [actual local persistence controls](../evidence/config-acceptance/author/nova-journal-binding-seam-identities-20261013.json)
  134 confirm these narrow current semantics, not future module binding.
  135 Its append-lock timeout is itself a current hardcoded policy candidate.
