  137 ### Proposed durable pre-dispatch transition (C5, not implemented)
  138 
  139 1. Pin R contract at new-run creation: graph/module/repair membership, grants,
  140    ceilings, effect identity, code/packages and live-module versus fixed mode.
  141 2. Under the existing run mutation/transaction boundary, look up the unique
  142    logical `(runId,moduleId)` or standalone operation key. Existing binding must
  143    recover its original closure; never supplement it from current author files.
  144 3. If unbound, select a complete validated generation once. Validate M eligibility
  145    against R; persist immutable content-addressed owner/profile/prompt objects and
  146    their complete file set, identities and secret revision references durably.
  147 4. Append/fsync the versioned binding before attempt/dispatch. Include generation,
  148    effective profile/instance mapping, input and original runpolicy/claim/deadline
  149    references. The binding introduces no independent budget counters.
  150 5. Dispatch from that closure. Technical retry, repair, wait/resume, cancellation,
  151    result reconciliation and cleanup inherit it with existing consumed budgets,
  152    cooldowns, deadlines and uncertain-effect states.
  153 
  154 Crash before step 4 permits selection without an effect; crash after binding but
  155 before dispatch recovers the same binding; crash after dispatch reconciles the
  156 real effect before repeating. Concurrent starts and publication linearize to a
  157 complete A or B, never mixed files. Started A remains A; eligible unbound module
  158 may use B; fixed Eval remains A. Invalid B fails before publication/dispatch, no
  159 silent fallback. Historical versioned runs drain/recover with original supported
